# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# codebase-memory-mcp code index
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The knowledge graph itself stays local. Full re-index of this repository
# takes ~30s, so every machine rebuilds it via scripts/cbm/bootstrap.* instead
# of carrying a binary through git history.
#
# Why not commit .codebase-memory/graph.db.zst?
#   It is ~16 MB and is rewritten on every index, including the file watcher's
#   incremental refreshes during normal editing. Git stores each rewrite as a
#   full new blob; upstream documents a team reaching ~6 GB of history on this
#   single path. Re-indexing is far cheaper than that history.
#
# To opt in (instant cold start on a fresh clone, at the cost of history size):
#   1. delete the next line
#   2. run:  scripts/cbm/bootstrap.ps1   (or bootstrap.sh)
#   3. commit .codebase-memory/ deliberately at milestones, not every save
#   For frequent updates, track it with Git LFS from the repo-root
#   .gitattributes instead:
#     .codebase-memory/graph.db.zst filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
.codebase-memory/

# Machine-specific MCP configuration written by scripts/cbm/bootstrap.*
# Absolute paths differ per machine, so these are regenerated, never shared.
# Committed AGENTS.md is what makes a fresh clone work before bootstrap runs.
.mcp.json
.cursor/mcp.json
.codex/config.toml

.claude
.codex
.cursor
.workbuddy

